@lang en
IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `nii-il33-nouns`

-- ===========================================================================
-- PUBLISHED FIGURES, NOT LAW. The consumer price index readings the updating clause of s 1 "הסכום הבסיסי"
-- reads. Row IL-33.
--
-- SOURCE. The Central Bureau of Statistics (CBS) of Israel, general consumer price index, code 120010, as the
-- CBS index API served it on 2026-10-08T22:27:03Z, deposited with the linkage coefficients at
--   ../../registers/source-bundle/data/cbs-cpi-general-120010-2000-01-to-2026-08-with-linkage-coefficients.json
--   sha256 cf440d64bf194af029f721149efa4fb1cbf7f1f73c2703e1c36d0589242b00f9
-- (and the same series without coefficients, sha256 11a1b271fd303b3109a761556ae2effb4aaa2e3762f9ac05886c10404e09eeb8).
-- Official CBS data; the latest reading is August 2026.
--
-- WHICH READINGS. The clause compares "the index published last before" a 1 January with "the index published
-- last before 1 January of the previous year". The CBS publishes the November index about 15 December, so for
-- a 1 January of year Y the readings are the November indices of Y-1 and of Y-2. Each is in the base in force
-- when it was published (a new base starts with the January index, published in February), so the two can be
-- in different bases. The first number is the November (Y-1) reading expressed in the base of the November
-- (Y-2) reading: the reading itself where the bases are the same, otherwise the CBS's linked value (the
-- `prevBase` entry of that reading in the coefficient file). The third number is the CBS's own twelve-month
-- change for the November (Y-1) reading, as the file prints it.
--
-- WHAT IS NOT DONE. No index is computed or estimated here: every number is copied from the file by a script
-- that reads the JSON. For a 1 January after 2026 the November index is not yet in the data and the function
-- is refused.
-- ===========================================================================

§ `Published figures — the CBS consumer price index (data, not law)`

-- Columns:            the later reading in the earlier base, the earlier reading, CBS twelve-month change (%)
@ref CBS general consumer price index 120010, deposited file sha256 cf440d64...b00f9
GIVEN year IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `The index readings for the update of a 1 January`
`the CBS index readings for the update of 1 January of` year MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF year EQUALS 2015 THEN `The index readings for the update of a 1 January` OF 102.1, 102.2, -0.1    -- Nov 2014: 102.1 (base 2012=100); Nov 2013: 102.2 (base 2012); CBS yoy -0.1%
        IF year EQUALS 2016 THEN `The index readings for the update of a 1 January` OF 101.184, 102.1, -0.9    -- Nov 2015: 99.2 (base 2014=100), linked to base 2012: 101.184; Nov 2014: 102.1 (base 2012); CBS yoy -0.9%
        IF year EQUALS 2017 THEN `The index readings for the update of a 1 January` OF 98.9, 99.2, -0.3    -- Nov 2016: 98.9 (base 2014=100); Nov 2015: 99.2 (base 2014); CBS yoy -0.3%
        IF year EQUALS 2018 THEN `The index readings for the update of a 1 January` OF 99.1967, 98.9, 0.3    -- Nov 2017: 100.3 (base 2016=100), linked to base 2014: 99.1967; Nov 2016: 98.9 (base 2014); CBS yoy 0.3%
        IF year EQUALS 2019 THEN `The index readings for the update of a 1 January` OF 101.5, 100.3, 1.2    -- Nov 2018: 101.5 (base 2016=100); Nov 2017: 100.3 (base 2016); CBS yoy 1.2%
        IF year EQUALS 2020 THEN `The index readings for the update of a 1 January` OF 101.808, 101.5, 0.3    -- Nov 2019: 100.8 (base 2018=100), linked to base 2016: 101.808; Nov 2018: 101.5 (base 2016); CBS yoy 0.3%
        IF year EQUALS 2021 THEN `The index readings for the update of a 1 January` OF 100.2, 100.8, -0.6    -- Nov 2020: 100.2 (base 2018=100); Nov 2019: 100.8 (base 2018); CBS yoy -0.6%
        IF year EQUALS 2022 THEN `The index readings for the update of a 1 January` OF 102.6069, 100.2, 2.4    -- Nov 2021: 102.3 (base 2020=100), linked to base 2018: 102.6069; Nov 2020: 100.2 (base 2018); CBS yoy 2.4%
        IF year EQUALS 2023 THEN `The index readings for the update of a 1 January` OF 107.7, 102.3, 5.3    -- Nov 2022: 107.7 (base 2020=100); Nov 2021: 102.3 (base 2020); CBS yoy 5.3%
        IF year EQUALS 2024 THEN `The index readings for the update of a 1 January` OF 111.3009, 107.7, 3.3    -- Nov 2023: 105.1 (base 2022=100), linked to base 2020: 111.3009; Nov 2022: 107.7 (base 2020); CBS yoy 3.3%
        IF year EQUALS 2025 THEN `The index readings for the update of a 1 January` OF 108.7, 105.1, 3.4    -- Nov 2024: 108.7 (base 2022=100); Nov 2023: 105.1 (base 2022); CBS yoy 3.4%
        IF year EQUALS 2026 THEN `The index readings for the update of a 1 January` OF 111.2664, 108.7, 2.4    -- Nov 2025: 103.6 (base 2024=100), linked to base 2022: 111.2664; Nov 2024: 108.7 (base 2022); CBS yoy 2.4%
        OTHERWISE REFUSE "the deposited CBS data gives the readings for the updates of 1 January 2015 to 1 January 2026 only: the November index of the year before is not in it"
